# Walkthrough: Command Center AI Fixes

The Command Center AI and Daily Brief generation have been restored by fixing critical backend code issues.

## Changes Made

### Backend

#### [brief_generator.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/brief_generator.py)
- **Implemented [_get_today_classes](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/brief_generator.py#149-174)**: This function was missing, causing a `NameError` (caught as "Brief generation failed" in the logs).
- **Fixed [Announcement](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/announcement.py#9-31) handling**: Ensured that the `course_code` for an announcement is derived from its related `Course` object, resolving an `AttributeError`.

#### [ai_tools.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_tools.py)
- **Updated [search_announcements](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_tools.py#114-135) and [search_assignments](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_tools.py#49-81)**: Fixed incorrect attribute access by properly joining with the `Course` table to retrieve `course_code`.

## Verification Results

### Success Confirmation
Brief generation was tested using a dedicated script and completed successfully.
The AI-generated content was correctly formatted and returned.

#### Test Execution
```bash
Testing brief generation for user: Oli (ID: 1)
✅ Brief generation succeeded!
Brief ID: 7
